PLANET='Sun'
COVER_SUB='What your Sun feels like in each sign.'
S=[
('Aries','Fire · cardinal','Exalted','The Sun is exalted in Aries: the equinox, where the days begin to outgrow the nights, and Jyotish places the Sun’s peak here too. It feels like a whirlwind: independence, a sharp mind, endless initiative and a will that wants to lead. Others may come to rely on you, though the pace is hot, sometimes chaotic, always trying to skip steps. Karmic astrology sees a soul learning to act alone and take its first step into form. The shadow is impatience and a despotic streak. The lesson: let the fire build something.'),
('Taurus','Earth · fixed','Venus’s sign','Taurus is a fixed sign ruled by Venus, and Jyotish counts Venus as an enemy of the Sun, so strength here is quiet. Energy is not wasted: you resist, endure and finish, and you are a better collaborator than commander. The old image is clay in a potter’s hands, order given to rough matter. You love the senses, the land, good food and steady money, with deep loyalty and a stubborn streak. Karmic reading: a soul learning self-worth without possession. The shadow is possessiveness. The lesson: what you value should serve you, not own you.'),
('Gemini','Air · mutable','Mercury’s sign','Gemini belongs to Mercury, neutral toward the Sun in Jyotish. The Sun here brings versatility and charm, a restless hunger for novelty and a sharp, critical, eclectic mind, good at analysis and synthesis. Short trips, research and conversation feed you; routine is unbearable. Anger is short and leaves no grudge. The old image is an agitated monkey, the lower kingdoms straining to become human. Karmic reading: a soul gathering experience before it chooses a direction. The shadow is scattered knowledge and frayed nerves. The lesson: depth comes from staying with one thing a little longer.'),
('Cancer','Water · cardinal','The Moon’s sign','Cancer is a tropical sign: the Sun turns at the summer solstice, and the sign belongs to the Moon, a friend of the Sun in Jyotish. The Sun is a guest here: gentle, charming, drawn to home, family and the past, with a rich imagination and a touch of indolence. The ancient image is a rounded boat, an ark of shelter and withdrawal. Karmic reading: a soul that enters life through family and memory, and must learn to build its own shelter. The shadow is clinging and living in the past. The lesson: a shell is for protection, not for hiding.'),
('Leo','Fire · fixed','The Sun’s own house','The Sun’s own house in every tradition: Jyotish calls it Simha, Surya’s own sign. Success comes through personality, a radiant, magnetic, generous presence with strong creativity and a passion that can overflow. The ancient image is a burst of light, like fireworks, radiating outward. It is the sign of the heart, as the Sun is the heart of the solar system. Karmic reading: a soul learning to shine and then to give that light to a group. The shadow is vanity and a wound when ignored. The lesson: a true king lights the room for others.'),
('Virgo','Earth · mutable','Mercury’s sign','Virgo is ruled by Mercury, neutral to the Sun in Jyotish. The Sun here gives excellent analysis and synthesis and sharp practical intuition. You seldom stand in front: you are the grey eminence who works quietly, modest, discreet and careful about health and work. The old image is the seed and the patient plowman. Karmic reading: a soul purifying itself through service and craft. The shadow is worry, over-criticism and neglecting yourself. The lesson: being useful does not require being flawless.'),
('Libra','Air · cardinal','Fall','Libra is the Sun’s fall, and Jyotish marks its lowest point at 10° (neecha); Venus, the ruler, is an enemy of the Sun there. The Sun here does not like to live alone and looks early for a stable partner. You love beauty, art and harmony, and your balance depends on relationship. Under strain, partnership and justice matters grow complicated. The old image is a keen arrow of sensation. Karmic reading: a soul learning to define itself apart from the other. The shadow is indecision. The lesson: peace that costs you yourself is not peace.'),
('Scorpio','Water · fixed','Mars’s sign','Scorpio belongs to Mars, a friend of the Sun in Jyotish, and to Pluto in modern astrology. A well-placed Sun here gives above-average intelligence, quick learning, a powerful imagination and strong intuition, with unseen help in times of need. Under strain it turns cold, calculating and obsessed with control. The old image is a den from which desire and passion shoot like arrows. Karmic reading: a soul passing through crisis, death and rebirth. The shadow is secrecy and jealousy. The lesson: every ending you survive teaches you how to begin again.'),
('Sagittarius','Fire · mutable','Jupiter’s sign','Sagittarius is ruled by Jupiter, friendly to the Sun in Jyotish, and is the third fire sign: ambition, savoir-faire, influential friends and success along the chosen path. There is a strong interest in humanities, law and teaching, in foreign countries and long stays abroad. The old image is restless movement toward more freedom, a harvest gathered on the way. Karmic reading: a soul seeking meaning, learning to turn belief into lived wisdom. The shadow is intolerance and preaching. The lesson: faith is stronger when it can tolerate a doubt.'),
('Capricorn','Earth · cardinal','Where the Sun turns','Capricorn is the winter solstice, where the Sun turns and the light starts to return. It belongs to Saturn, an enemy of the Sun in Jyotish, so the Sun works under pressure and grows stronger with time. Longevity, endurance and a granite will: you are prudent, thoughtful and never lose sight of the goal, with a taste for solitude and demanding study. The old image is an upright figure projected toward the future, like a pregnant woman. Karmic reading: a soul building structure and taking responsibility. The shadow is coldness. The lesson: authority is stronger when it is human.'),
('Aquarius','Air · fixed','Opposite the Sun’s house','Aquarius is Saturn’s other house, opposite Leo, so the Sun feels out of place; Jyotish also counts Saturn as an enemy. It gives moral and intellectual quality, nonconformism, a taste for avant-garde science and a strong sense of friendship. Under strain it shows eccentricity, utopian ideas and a lonely end. The old image is a birth, a tear in the veil through which the new is carried. Karmic reading: a soul learning to serve a group without losing itself. The shadow is detachment. The lesson: belonging to a group does not mean dissolving in it.'),
('Pisces','Water · mutable','Jupiter’s sign','Pisces belongs to Jupiter, a friend of the Sun in Jyotish, and to Neptune in modern astrology. The Sun here has deep, uncommon sensitivity: you worry about a thousand things, then withdraw to avoid feeling other people’s suffering. Dream, music, art and contact with the invisible world are your gifts. The old image is something soft and dissolving, a farewell. Karmic reading: a soul at the end of a long cycle, learning compassion and release. The shadow is escape from reality. The lesson: kindness needs a shore to stand on.'),
]
